<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lúrio River</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Lúrio is a river in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mozambique">Mozambique</a> that flows about 600 km east from the Niassa highlands to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indian-ocean">Indian Ocean</a>. For much of its course it separates Niassa and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cape-delgado">Cabo Delgado</a> provinces to the north from Nampula province to the south. From 1891 it marked the southern limit of the territory granted to the Niassa Company.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lurio-river.jpg" alt="Lúrio River" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Hans Braxmeier &amp;amp; Peter in s, Location map:NordNordWest · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rivers_of_northern_Mozambique_OSM.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
